A||||3||DecadenceR||Pushrod cover||||1||
Z||000000||DecadenceR||07-21-2001||07:47 PM||||Is it possible to remove the pushrod cover, under the intake on a 4cyl, without removing the intake? Well, I'm sure it's possible, but is it possible AND worth any extra effort?<BR>I have an oil leak coming from that cover, and I need to fix it. I'd like to not tear apart the whole motor again.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||07-21-2001||11:57 PM||||It won't be fun but it should come off. I think you'll at least need to remove the alternator to get to one end. Removing the oil filter may give you some extra room to work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DecadenceR||07-22-2001||01:54 AM||||OK, thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||07-22-2001||04:05 AM||||Mine had studs holding the cover on, I had a tuff time with it and was afraid I had let some of the old gasket fall in the lifter area. You can't see very much with the manifold in place. Didn't matter anyway, a week later I clogged the oil pump screen while cleaning off an inch of crud on top of the head. That's when the stuff hit the fan & Hooker Auto repair got my vacation $ for an overhaul.Just thought I'd throw that in,SINCE JANE THROWS IT AT ME ALMOST EVERY WEEK! sorry, all done now,too much caffein,time to go nighty night.||||reg||1
